<GlazePolicyLayout title="Glaze Privacy — Your grades aren't a business model" description="Always free. No Pro tier, telemetry, data sales or advertising profiles. Read Glaze's privacy promise, local storage details and optional encrypted-sharing disclosures." page="privacy">
  <header class="policy-hero">
    <div class="policy-hero-copy">
      <p class="policy-kicker"><span class="policy-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span> Privacy, by principle</p>
      <h1>Your grades aren't<br />a <em>business model.</em></h1>
      <p class="policy-lead">Your education is expensive enough. Your sidebar doesn't need a subscription. And your coursework doesn't belong in somebody else's analytics dashboard.</p>
      <div class="policy-pills"><span>No telemetry</span><span>No data sales</span><span>No Pro. Ever.</span></div>
      <p class="policy-date">Privacy policy · Updated <time datetime="2026-10-29">October 29, 2026</time></p>
    </div>
    <div class="privacy-orbit" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="orbit-ring orbit-ring-one"></div><div class="orbit-ring orbit-ring-two"></div>
      <div class="orbit-core"><svg viewBox="0 0 64 64" fill="none"><path d="M32 7 52 15v16c0 13-13 22-20 26-7-4-20-13-20-26V15L32 7Z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/><path d="m23 31 6 6 13-14" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>YOURS.</span></div>
      <span class="orbit-label orbit-label-one">on your device</span><span class="orbit-label orbit-label-two">under your control</span>
      <span class="orbit-spark spark-one"></span><span class="orbit-spark spark-two"></span>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="promise-grid" aria-label="Our permanent commitments">
    <div><span class="promise-number">01</span><h2>Never for sale.</h2><p>We never sell, rent or broker your personal data. We never share it for advertising, profiling or AI training.</p></div>
    <div><span class="promise-number">02</span><h2>No surveillance.</h2><p>No product analytics, tracking pixels, session replay or engagement reporting to Frostdev. No student profiles for schools or advertisers.</p></div>
    <div><span class="promise-number">03</span><h2>Always free.</h2><p>No subscriptions. No trials that turn into bills. No Pro tier. No feature unlocks you have to pay for. Now or later.</p></div>
  </section>

  <aside class="policy-plain" aria-label="What this promise means">
    <strong>Privacy is a promise we have to explain honestly.</strong>
    <p>Glaze processes school data on your device to show your work. It doesn't send that coursework to Frostdev for collection or analysis. If you choose encrypted sharing, selected encrypted content goes to a relay. If you turn on AI, the features you allow send what they need to the AI provider or address you chose. If you connect an AI app through Agents, it gets only what you allow. Browser sync, hosting and connections you choose also process some information. Those boundaries are here in the open—not buried in an asterisk.</p>
  </aside>

  <div class="policy-body">
    <nav class="policy-contents" aria-label="Privacy contents"><span>THE DETAILS</span><a href="#local">On your device</a><a href="#connections">Connections you choose</a><a href="#sharing">Encrypted sharing</a><a href="#website">Visiting this site</a><a href="#control">Your controls</a><a href="#promise">Keeping the promise</a></nav>
    <div class="policy-reading">
      <section id="local">
        <p class="policy-kicker">01 / Local means local</p><h2>Your work lives with you.</h2>
        <p>This policy covers the official Glaze extension and its optional sharing service, developed by Frostdev. The <a href="/privacy">Frostdev website and other services</a> have their own disclosures. Your school and browser provider also have their own policies.</p>
        <p>Glaze reads supported Blackboard Ultra, Canvas and Moodle pages and their school-hosted APIs using your existing school session. It processes course names, assignments, dates, grades and submission state for the features you use. We do not receive a copy of that school content on Frostdev servers for analytics or reporting. Glaze does not ask for your school password or create a Glaze account.</p>
        <div class="policy-table-wrap" id="what-glaze-stores" role="region" aria-label="Local storage details" tabindex="0"><table><caption>What stays in your extension</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Data</th><th scope="col">Purpose and location</th></tr></thead><tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">Notes, tasks, plans and imported documents</th><td>Local extension storage and IndexedDB. Document text extraction happens on your device; saved fields are the ones you review. A syllabus goes to AI only if you turn AI on for Syllabus import.</td></tr>
          <tr id="glaze-writer"><th scope="row">Glaze Writer papers and documents</th><td>Assignment papers and the documents you start or import on Documents, with their versions, your format presets, personal dictionary and saved sources, stay in extension storage on this device. Spreadsheets keep their cells, and PDFs and PowerPoint decks keep the file itself (up to 50 MB each), in the extension’s own storage in this browser; Glaze reads and draws them there and sends them nowhere. They are never synced, and Glaze keeps no copy on a server. Delete moves a paper or document to Trash, which removes it for good after 30 days when the browser next starts or Documents opens, unless you restore it first. <strong>Back up…</strong> includes them, a spreadsheet with its cells and a PDF or deck with its file; uninstalling removes them. Writer keeps no copy of what you type in a discussion, message or test box; Back up what you type does, when it is on. The thread, prompt, rubric and files Writer reads for a box stay in that page's memory.</td></tr>
          <tr id="agents-records"><th scope="row">Agents</th><td>App identities, pairing and last-use times, group grants and declines, the Agents switch and profile id stay on this device. So do the last 200 calls’ metadata (never their contents) and the 100 assignment reads used last, without timed expiry. Session-only approval records can include document text. <strong>Turn off</strong> ends connections, cancels waiting requests and clears assignment reads; apps and grants stay, and a change already started can finish. <strong>Revoke</strong> forgets one app; <strong>Forget all apps</strong> forgets every app and clears the activity list and assignment reads. Both keep the switch and profile id. Removing a site clears its assignment reads. Uninstalling the extension leaves the helper and copies an app kept. <code>npx glaze-mcp uninstall</code> removes owned setup files and unchanged helper copies; it leaves the run folder and modified copies.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Grades, what-if scores, GPA and Insights</th><td>Local calculations and cached school data. Insights is optional, runs on your device and is not a report sent to us or your school.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Settings and course appearance</th><td>Your browser's extension storage. With Chrome sync enabled, supported preferences—including course nicknames and appearance—can pass through your browser provider. Safari keeps these locally.</td></tr>
          <tr id="the-sidebar"><th scope="row">Sidebar and dock</th><td>Width, open/fold state, To Do scope, widget destinations, order and heights stay on this device, per school and account. General settings, including the title and appearance, can sync. Reset sidebar keeps widget destinations, dock order and data. The sidebar stores none of the native panels' text or grades and adds no request for them.</td></tr>
          <tr id="fresh-install-defaults"><th scope="row">Starter layouts and removals</th><td>New installs get pet, timer, notes, quote and course-card widgets, with To Do and settings in the first sidebar. Setup records and layouts stay local. Choices that keep removed defaults from returning can sync and include school origins, course ids or the sidebar's account id.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Course tabs and sketches</th><td>Saved course URLs and scroll positions are local. Canvas also retains earlier pages and forms in memory; browser history holds frame/course ids and page URLs. Blurred stand-ins use sketches of page boxes, colors and the course name, with no other text or images. Sketches stay in memory or extension session storage, not our servers, and clear on browser close, sign-out or turning tabs off.</td></tr>
          <tr id="document-review"><th scope="row">Document review</th><td>Glaze reads the existing page's structure, title, grade/feedback/rubric elements and viewer address to arrange the view. It saves no document or grade content and makes no request to the viewer's origin. Preferences can sync. Optional Remember focus keeps only a focus flag keyed by the submission page path in the school's tab session storage until it closes; the school page can read it.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Draft backups and study history</th><td>Device-local recovery and features you enable. Typing backups expire within 14 days, including unfinished sidebar To Do forms when Back up what you type is on. Without backup, those forms stay in document memory. Reminders, streaks and the pet do not send us activity events.</td></tr>
        </tbody></table></div>
        <p>Course tabs open real school pages, so those pages still make their normal requests. <span id="adding-a-schools-own-site">Glaze runs on Blackboard, Canvas and Moodle's own domains and on school sites you allow;</span> <strong>Settings → Privacy and data → Sites</strong> lists them. That access is not permission for us to collect general browsing history. School scripts can read information displayed inside school pages, including an open note. Glaze cannot make your school's own page private from your school.</p>
        <p>Canvas can cache its course-list answers, including scores, enrollments and your account id, in the school's tab session storage. Glaze reuses them for less than a minute after checking the account; they can remain until the tab closes and are readable by the school page. The settings session copy holds only what the first paint shows, with no course names or nicknames, picture or link addresses, sidebar title or review choices. Document review's frame relay carries only bar visibility controls, checks the school origin and sending window, and accepts review requests only from the current visible same-account frame.</p>
        <p>The <a href={`${source}/blob/main/PRIVACY.md`}>release-specific technical policy</a> lists storage fields, limits, retention and requests in detail. The <a href={source}>source code</a> is public.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="connections">
        <p class="policy-kicker">02 / No secret destinations</p><h2>A connection should have a reason.</h2>
        <ul class="policy-list">
          <li><strong>Your school:</strong> local helpers read your school's data there. Glaze never changes real grades. On Blackboard, Glaze Writer reads a box's prompt, thread and rubric, and for Feedback the assignment's attached files, read-only. Your words reach Blackboard only when you press its Post, Reply, Send or Submit: Ctrl/⌘+Enter presses Post, Reply or Send, and Writer's submit sheet attaches your paper's .docx, or the PDF, deck or .xlsx open in its place, through Blackboard's upload and clicks its Submit once. <strong>Open in Glaze</strong> beside an assignment's attached PDF, deck or spreadsheet reads that file from your Blackboard site when you click it. The optional Canvas planner-tick setting can update a planner done mark, including one an agent app asks for and you allow; Ultra ticks stay local. Changing a course nickname or color in its Canvas card menu saves that choice to Canvas. Sign out in Glaze’s Canvas bar signs you out of Canvas, and Moodle’s Edit mode switch drives Moodle’s own control.</li>
          <li><strong>Fonts, images and music:</strong> opening the font list loads small previews; choosing a web font downloads it from its font provider. Linked images and music players contact the provider you choose. The Documents page loads your Look's web font the same way. Those services see ordinary request metadata and may use their own cookies.</li>
          <li id="agent-access"><strong id="agents">Agents, off by default:</strong> <strong>Settings → AI → Agents</strong> lets AI apps on your computer, such as Claude Desktop, reach Glaze through a helper on this computer: <code>glaze-mcp</code> for Chrome, Edge, the other Chromium browsers and Firefox, and the downloaded Glaze Mac app for Safari (the Mac App Store app has no agent access). The helper relays messages through a local socket (a named pipe on Windows) with a random token, opens no network connections and saves no message contents. On Chrome, Edge, other Chromium browsers and Firefox, turning Agents on asks to let Glaze start the helper; Firefox also asks to share website content in that prompt. Turning Agents off gives those permissions back. Safari has helper permission from installation. An app gets nothing until you allow it in Glaze’s window, per app and per group: courses, to-dos and schedule; grades; assignments and rubrics; Writer documents; each mod’s tools. An app names itself, and other programs on your account can reach the helper, so a reported name is not proof of who an app is. School data comes from dated Canvas and Blackboard Ultra caches, refreshed where possible through your open school tab. Reading an assignment uses that tab or its last saved read: instructions, attached file names and rubric, never your scores or feedback. Every built-in change waits for your OK, in Glaze’s own words: marking a to-do done (with <strong>Tick off in Canvas too</strong> on, also in your Canvas planner), inserting a citation or applying a fix in Writer. Glaze’s built-in agent tools never submit work, post, send messages or change grades. Every call to a mod’s code tool waits for your OK too. It runs with that mod’s permissions, which can include sending data to its approved hosts; the app’s group grants do not narrow them. Glaze sends nothing to Frostdev; the app may send what it gets to its own AI service, under that app’s policy. Details: the <a href="/guides/glaze-agents">Agents guide</a>.</li>
          <li id="citation-lookups"><strong>Citation lookups:</strong> only when you click Look up in Writer's Cite: a DOI to <code>doi.org</code> (or <code>api.crossref.org</code> and <code>data.crosscite.org</code>), an ISBN to <code>openlibrary.org</code>, a web address to that page's own host once you allow it. No cookies or referrer are sent, and only a source you save is kept. If you enable AI Feedback and the page lacks citation details, its address and text can also go to your Feedback model.</li>
          <li id="ai-providers"><strong>AI, off by default:</strong> only when you turn it on in Settings → AI and allow a feature, that feature sends what it needs to the provider you connected (OpenAI, Anthropic, Google Gemini, OpenRouter, xAI, Mistral, Groq or DeepSeek) or an OpenAI-compatible address you added. A model on this device sends nothing. Syllabus import sends the syllabus. Writer's Tab completion sends your text before and after the caret, the course, the prompt or assignment, and in a discussion your classmates' posts with their names; its other AI tools send your draft or the part they check, with the assignment's instructions, rubric and attached files for Feedback. AI outline sends document sections and the interface language; AI source extraction sends bibliography entries. Both start on when AI is enabled and a Feedback model is configured, with separate switches in Settings → AI. Their labels and source details stay locally with the paper. With Feedback on, an open assignment’s pictures can be read before you ask; readings stay on this device for up to 30 days, with at most 128 cached entries. Nothing goes to AI from a test or quiz. Keys stay on this device, never synced, backed up or given to a page. Glaze runs no AI server; each provider has its own policy.</li>
          <li id="the-looks-gallery"><strong>Looks and Mods gallery:</strong> the gallery is a website you visit yourself. Glaze asks it only for the one background file or mod you choose there, when you click to use it.</li>
          <li><strong>Report a problem:</strong> opens a new GitHub issue with your Glaze version, browser, system and language filled in, and nothing about your school. GitHub receives that text when the page opens; nothing is posted until you submit it.</li>
          <li><strong>Gradescope:</strong> only after enabling it and approving the account/course mapping, Glaze reads that site's work into your device-local planner. No Gradescope password is stored.</li>
          <li><strong>Downloads and updates:</strong> browser stores and GitHub deliver the extension. The Safari app checks Frostdev's update feed and downloads updates from GitHub. Those servers necessarily process network requests.</li>
          <li><strong>Exports:</strong> files are created on your device. What happens after you send a file or import a calendar elsewhere is your choice, under that recipient's policy.</li>
          <li id="user-installed-mods"><strong>Mods you install:</strong> course data requires declared and granted permissions. On Chrome, code with access to personal data runs in a Worker. The <code>nav.read</code> permission also grants personal data: navigation labels, course names, unread counts and navigation events, without link addresses, and disables the mod's frame UI. A mod granted both data and network access can send that data to its approved hosts. Separate permissions let it manage up to eight items with school-site links or click actions, or propose a layout while it runs. <strong>Use my own</strong> keeps that mod's layouts off locally. On the Documents page, in its own tab, <code>documents</code> lets a mod read your documents' titles, courses and word counts and add items of its own; <code>documents.read</code> adds their text and exported files. Both count as personal data. Firefox and Safari use declarative parts only.</li>
          <li id="signed-mod-blocklist"><strong>Signed mod blocklist:</strong> on Chrome, when Glaze and this optional setting are on and a code mod is installed, Glaze makes a credential-free check at most daily. Failed checks retry after an hour. The host receives ordinary connection metadata. Declarative-only mods, Firefox and Safari do not make this request.</li>
          <li><strong>Google Calendar:</strong> sync is unavailable while Google verification is pending. Local calendar-file export remains available without connecting Google.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We do not add analytics to these connections. Browser and provider services have their own privacy practices. Features that aren't available in your release are not enabled by this policy.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="sharing">
        <p class="policy-kicker">03 / Sharing is your verb</p><h2 id="optional-encrypted-share-sessions">You choose the audience.<br />We don't get the key.</h2>
        <p>Sharing starts off. Create, Join or Resume connects only when you choose it. Selected notes, tasks, Looks and attachments are encrypted on your device before they reach the relay you select. Your school assignments and account identifiers are not included as shared content. Local tools work fully without a sharing server.</p>
        <p>Encryption keys live in the invitation's fragment and in your extension. The relay receives encrypted bytes, random identifiers, signatures, sizes and connection metadata. Its network infrastructure can see IP addresses and timing. The default relay uses Cloudflare infrastructure; a custom operator controls its own hosting, logs and backups. This is necessary service processing, not a student analytics program. We do not sell it or use it for advertising or profiling.</p>
        <p><strong>Keep invitations and backups private.</strong> Anyone with a link's key can access that session at the link's permission level. Backups (<strong>Back up…</strong>, and older settings files and Notes ZIPs) include share keys and creator delete tokens for all sessions, including paused ones; someone with a creator token may delete a session. Single-note exports do not contain session keys. Opening an invitation in a browser can leave its fragment in browser history.</p>
        <p>Pause stops new session traffic. Leave keeps your local copies. Creator deletion removes the live session. The default relay removes a share after two unused years, or one year if its creator chooses, and an empty share after two unused days. Recipients' copies and older operator backups are not erased by that action. Removed items can remain in encrypted history until compaction. If a disclosure is legally required, we can provide only information we actually hold; we cannot provide encryption keys we never received.</p>
        <p><a href={`${source}/blob/main/server/README.md`}>Run your own relay</a> or read the <a href={`${source}/blob/main/PRIVACY.md#optional-encrypted-share-sessions`}>full sharing and retention details</a>.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="website">
        <p class="policy-kicker">04 / This page counts too</p><h2>No invisible audience.</h2>
        <p>These Glaze pages have no analytics scripts, tracking pixels, session replay or advertising scripts. The existing AdSense ownership tag and ads.txt file identify the website publisher; they do not load an ad or run an advertising tracker. These pages will not become an advertising funnel for your school activity.</p>
        <p>Hosting, Cloudflare and ordinary web-server security logs can process your IP address, requested URL and browser headers to deliver and protect the site. We do not pretend that an internet request contains no data. We do not join that metadata to your coursework or use it to build advertising profiles. See the <a href="/privacy">website policy</a> and <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare's policy</a>.</p>
        <p>If you email us, we receive the address and message you send so we can answer. Please leave passwords, student identifiers and coursework out of support requests; redact screenshots. We keep support correspondence only as needed to handle the request or meet legal obligations, and do not add it to a marketing list.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="control">
        <p class="policy-kicker">05 / You hold the controls</p><h2>Off means off. Yours means yours.</h2>
        <p>Disable individual helpers or Glaze as a whole, pause sharing, remove a site in <strong>Settings → Privacy and data → Sites</strong> or revoke browser site access, clear local feature records or uninstall. We cannot remotely read or erase device-only records. Uninstalling or clearing browser storage can erase your local work: use <strong>Back up…</strong> in Settings → Privacy and data before moving or removing the extension.</p>
        <p>Local notes, papers and documents in Trash expire after 30 days; reminder and recovery records have their own documented expiry. Other local records can remain until you clear them, replace them or remove Glaze. Deletion markers may be kept temporarily to stop old saves restoring deleted work. <a href={`${source}/blob/main/PRIVACY.md`}>Exact retention by feature</a> is published with the code.</p>
        <p>Contact <a href="mailto:admin@frostdev.io">admin@frostdev.io</a> for access, correction or deletion of information Frostdev actually holds. A self-hosted relay has its own operator. We don't sell or use personal information for cross-context behavioral advertising, so there is no data-sale toggle you need to hunt down.</p>
        <p>Glaze does not ask for a date of birth or create child accounts. Follow your school's rules and the requirements of your browser and services. Tell us if you believe a child has sent personal information to us; we will address the request without asking you to post it publicly.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="promise">
        <p class="policy-kicker">06 / A commitment, not a campaign</p><h2>No “for now” in the promise.</h2>
        <p>Glaze will remain free. We will not introduce Pro, Premium, subscriptions or paid feature gates. We will not add data sales, product tracking, advertising profiles or AI training on your content as the price of using it. Optional sharing is for the people you invite, not for us to monetize.</p>
        <p>We will date and publish policy updates when features or technical processing change. An update will not turn these commitments into an opt-out checkbox or a license to sell data. This policy is a promise about the official Glaze product; your rights under its <a href={`${source}/blob/main/LICENSE`}>MIT license</a> remain intact.</p>
        <a class="policy-text-link" href="/glaze/terms">Read the terms. There isn't a payment section. <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</GlazePolicyLayout>
